# Line endings for a WoW addon team working on both macOS and Windows.
# Copy this file to the root of every addon repository. Inside
# wow-forever-toolkit it applies to the devsetup/ folder.
#
# Why LF everywhere (evidence in handson_xplat.md):
# - The game loads CRLF and LF files alike. The BigWigs packager writes CRLF by
#   default and Mac players run those zips (BigWigs v427.6 is CRLF only).
# - The packager rewrites .lua .md .toc .txt .xml line endings on output anyway
#   (CRLF by default, LF with -u), so repository line endings never reach players.
# - Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true. Without this file a Windows
#   checkout gets CRLF, and bash scripts then fail with "$'\r': command not found".
# - Fixing LF in the repository keeps diffs clean between Mac and Windows users.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.lua    text eol=lf
*.toc    text eol=lf
*.xml    text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
.pkgmeta text eol=lf
# PowerShell 5.1 and 7 run LF scripts; keep .ps1 files ASCII-only (5.1 reads
# BOM-less files in the ANSI code page).
*.ps1    text eol=lf
# cmd.exe batch files are the one exception.
*.cmd    text eol=crlf
*.bat    text eol=crlf

# Game assets and archives: never convert.
*.blp    binary
*.tga    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.ogg    binary
*.mp3    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.zip    binary
